,"fullName":"Sen. Kelly, Mark [D-AZ]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-28","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AZ"},{"bioguideId":"G000574","fullName":"Sen. Gallego, Ruben [D-AZ]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AZ"},{"bioguideId":"L000577","fullName":"Sen. Lee, Mike [R-UT]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-19","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"UT"},{"bioguideId":"L000575","fullName":"Sen. Lankford, James [R-OK]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OK"},{"bioguideId":"C001095","fullName":"Sen. Cotton, Tom [R-AR]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AR"},{"bioguideId":"W000800","fullName":"Sen. Welch, Peter [D-VT]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-12-01","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VT"},{"bioguideId":"H001076","fullName":"Sen. Hassan, Margaret Wood [D-NH]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-12-02","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NH"},{"bioguideId":"C001113","fullName":"Sen. Cortez Masto, Catherine [D-NV]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-01-12","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NV"},{"bioguideId":"K000384","fullName":"Sen. Kaine, Tim [D-VA]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-01-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"},{"bioguideId":"G000555","fullName":"Sen. Gillibrand, Kirsten E. [D-NY]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-03-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NY"},{"bioguideId":"R000618","fullName":"Sen. Ricketts, Pete [R-NE]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-03-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NE"},{"bioguideId":"B001243","fullName":"Sen. Blackburn, Marsha [R-TN]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-03-11","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TN"},{"bioguideId":"W000802","fullName":"Sen. Whitehouse, Sheldon [D-RI]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-03-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"RI"},{"bioguideId":"D000563","fullName":"Sen. Durbin, Richard J. [D-IL]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IL"},{"bioguideId":"C001088","fullName":"Sen. Coons, Christopher A. [D-DE]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-05-11","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"DE"},{"bioguideId":"B001288","fullName":"Sen. Booker, Cory A. [D-NJ]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-06-01","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NJ"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-10-05T19:01:26+00:00","id":"s3062-119","introducedDate":"2025-10-28","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-05-11","text":"Placed on Senate Legislative Calendar under General Orders. Calendar No. 406."},"laws":[],"number":"3062","originChamber":"Senate","policyArea":"Crime and Law Enforcement","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"H001089","district":null,"fullName":"Sen. Hawley, Josh [R-MO]","party":"R","state":"MO"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2026-05-11","actionDesc":"Reported to Senate","text":"<p><strong>Guidelines for User Age-verification and Responsible Dialogue Act of 2026 or the GUARD Act</strong></p><p>This bill establishes requirements for and limitations on entities that provide publicly available&nbsp;artificial intelligence (AI) chatbots, including AI companions.</p><p>Under the bill, an&nbsp;<em>AI chatbot</em> is an application or program that simulates human conversation by generating responses to user prompts. An <em>AI companion</em> is a type of AI chatbot that simulates a sustained interpersonal relationship or emotional interaction with the user.</p><p>The bill makes it a federal crime to provide an AI&nbsp;chatbot&nbsp;that exposes minors to sexual content or encourages minors to commit suicide or carry out nonsuicidal self-injury, unlawful physical or sexual violence, or homicide. A violation is subject to a criminal fine of up to $250,000 per offense.</p><p>Additionally, the bill prohibits minors from accessing AI companions. Under the bill, an entity that provides an AI chatbot must require each individual who accesses an AI companion to set up a user account and must also verify that the user is an adult. A violation is subject to a civil penalty of up to $250,000 per violation.</p><p>Finally, the bill requires an AI chatbot that is publicly available&nbsp;to disclose that the AI chatbot is not a human and is not a licensed professional (e.g. doctor, lawyer, or therapist). A violation is subject to a civil penalty of up to $250,000 per violation.</p>","updateDate":"2026-10-05T15:42:52Z","versionCode":"25"}],"title":"GUARD Act","type":"s","updateDate":"2026-10-05T15:55:51Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-10-05T15:55:51Z"}
